From ab359f9b3f0ff809755f20ee84410de45a61be47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:15:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Launch: sign-in limits count the person, not the room's
 address

The 21 Oct launch puts a hundred people on one room's Wi-Fi; the auth routes
allowed 30 requests per five minutes per IP, about ten people's sign-up, and
OTP sends fell back to the IP for apps with no device id (the tester's 60292).
Misho, 15 Oct: key them to the phone and device. Each sign-in step now counts
per person (X-Device-Id, else the body's phone, else the IP) at the old 30,
with a per-address cap of 300 as the abuse guard; OTP sends stay at five per
person per ten minutes. The limiter gains keyBy 'person' and 'ip'.

